(This doesn't seem to have made it out the first time; I may have
accidentally posted it to a moderated group.  This version also includes
some late responses.)

The straw poll results have been received.  The CFV will soon go out,
with the proposal to move rec.games.rogue to rec.games.roguelike.rogue.

The CFV was to include proposals 1 and 2, and either 3A or 3B; the
purpose of the straw poll was to decide between 3A and 3B.

Proposal 1: Move rec.games.hack to rec.games.roguelike.nethack.
Proposal 2: Move rec.games.moria to rec.games.roguelike.moria.

Proposal 3A: Move rec.games.rogue to rec.games.roguelike.rogue.
Proposal 3B: Move rec.games.rogue to the existing group 
rec.games.roguelike.misc.

With 28 responses received, the vote was 17 for proposal 3A, 10 for
proposal 3B, and 1 with no opinion.  Proposal 3A had majority support
from both readers and non-readers of rec.games.rogue.

There was also more strong opposition to proposal 3B.  Nine of the 17
who preferred 3A said that they would vote differently, and six of those
nine said that they would vote for 3A but against 3B.  Only three of the
ten who preferred 3B said that they would vote for 3B and abstain from
3A, or abstain from 3B and vote against 3A, and nobody said that he or
she would vote for 3B but against 3A.

